### 1. Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Snehal",
  "email": "snehal@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 2. Login to obtain JWT Token
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "snehal@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Store token from login response above:
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 3. Get all tasks for current user
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4. Create a new task
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Java Full Stack Project",
  "description": "Build the TaskFlow task management system with Spring Boot & React",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15"
}

### 5. Get task by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6. Update task by ID
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Java Full Stack Project (Updated)",
  "description": "Testing and deployment complete",
  "status": "COMPLETED",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-15"
}

### 7. Delete task by ID
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}